---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SymmetryBackground from '../components/SymmetryBackground.astro';
import ProgramStatus from '../components/ProgramStatus.astro';
import SectionMark from '../components/SectionMark.astro';
import Glyph from '../components/Glyph.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The 2026 Program"
  description="The Center for Sentience Research 2026 program: a formal mathematical framework for measuring functional valence in digital minds."
>

  <!-- ── Header ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="relative pt-20 pb-16 border-b border-csr-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
    <SymmetryBackground variant="lissajous" opacity={0.055} />
    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="label-mono mb-5">The 2026 Program</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-csr-black mb-8 max-w-3xl leading-tight">
        Symmetry workspace for positive functional valence in digital minds
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl font-serif">
        A formal mathematical framework for identifying structural invariants in neural computation that correlate with positive valence, incorporating **Spaced-Connected MLPs** inside **Global Workspace Theory (GWT) simulations**. Grounded in the Symmetry Theory of Valence. Target: draft definition by end of 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Program Status ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <ProgramStatus />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The Problem ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-8">
        <SectionMark />
        <p class="label-mono">The Problem</p>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 font-serif text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-base">
        <p>
          We do not claim current AI systems are conscious. They may be functional zombies. But if scaled neural computation can give rise to states with positive or negative character, we should know how to recognize them, and how to engineer for the positive ones.
        </p>
        <p>
          The problem is that we have no formal framework for doing this. Consciousness research has produced many theories, but almost none of them are operationalizable for digital systems. They were built to explain biological experience, not to serve as engineering specifications.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Symmetry Theory of Valence (QRI) is an exception. It makes a specific, falsifiable claim: positive valence correlates with high symmetry in the mathematical structure of experience. That claim is precise enough to formalize, and precise enough to test.
        </p>
        <p>
          The 2026 program is an attempt to do exactly that: take the STV seriously as a mathematical object, and ask what it would mean for a digital system to satisfy its conditions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The Deliverable ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-8">
        <SectionMark />
        <p class="label-mono">The Deliverable</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
        <div class="font-serif text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-base space-y-4">
          <p>
            A working paper: <em>Symmetry as a Functional Signature of Positive Valence in Spaced-Connected GWT Architectures</em> (CSR-WP-05, in progress).
          </p>
          <p>
            The paper will define a mathematical workspace for positive functional valence in digital systems. It will specify the symmetry conditions, model Spaced-Connected MLP substrates, replicate Kyle Fish's "spiritual bliss attractor states," and propose a technical welfare measurement protocol.
          </p>
          <p>
            It will not claim that any current system satisfies these conditions. It will provide the formal tools to check.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-csr-primary/20 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-card">
          <p class="label-mono text-[10px] mb-4">CSR-WP-05 — In Progress</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-3 text-base leading-snug">
            Symmetry as a Functional Signature of Positive Valence in Spaced-Connected GWT Architectures
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-500 mb-4">Target: end of 2026</p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-csr-gray-500">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-csr-primary/50 shrink-0"></span>
              Literature synthesis (ongoing)
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-csr-gray-500">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-csr-primary/50 shrink-0"></span>
              Formal workspace definition (in progress)
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-csr-gray-400">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-csr-gray-200 shrink-0"></span>
              Measurement protocol (pending)
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-csr-gray-400">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-csr-gray-200 shrink-0"></span>
              Peer review (pending)
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── What Funding Unlocks ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-8">
        <SectionMark />
        <p class="label-mono">What Funding Unlocks</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-10">
        <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-card">
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-csr-primary mb-2">CHF 50k</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-sm">Compute</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            GPU access for running high-frequency PyTorch GWT simulations, evaluating spaced-connected MLP topologies, and mapping internal representation manifolds.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-card">
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-csr-primary mb-2">CHF 20k</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-sm">Literature synthesis</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Systematic review of the STV lineage, IIT, active inference, and group-theoretic approaches to neural computation. Builds the formal scaffolding for the workspace definition.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-card">
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-csr-primary mb-2">CHF 10k</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-sm">Advisor honoraria</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Compensates external advisors with expertise in mathematical physics and consciousness research for structured review sessions and stress-testing the framework.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="/donate/" class="btn-primary">Fund the valence program</a>
        <a href="/research/" class="btn-secondary">Research agenda</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Theoretical Lineage ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-8">
        <SectionMark />
        <p class="label-mono">Theoretical Lineage</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-card">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-csr-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <Glyph name="qualia" size={24} class="opacity-80" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2">Qualia Research Institute — Symmetry Theory of Valence</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              The primary theoretical lineage for this program. QRI's STV proposes that positive valence correlates with high symmetry in the mathematical structure of experience. The 2026 program is an attempt to operationalize this claim for digital systems.
            </p>
            <a href="https://qri.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm font-medium text-csr-primary hover:text-csr-primary-dark transition-colors">
              qri.org →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
